---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_DOMAIN, SITE_URL, LAST_UPDATED, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../config/siteInfo';

const pageTitle = `Privacy Policy — ${SITE_NAME}`;
const pageDescription = `Privacy Policy for ${SITE_DOMAIN}. Independent browser-based software project. No sale or sharing of personal data. U.S. CCPA/CPRA, COPPA (15 U.S.C. §§ 6501–6506), and state privacy law compliant.`;
const canonicalURL = `${SITE_URL}/privacy-policy/`;
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} canonicalURL={canonicalURL}>
  <main class="ror-main">
    <div class="ror-container">
      <div class="ror-back-row">
        <a href="/" class="ror-back-link">&larr; Back to {SITE_NAME}</a>
      </div>

      <h1 class="ror-h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="ror-updated">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">Overview</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          <strong class="ror-strong">{SITE_NAME}</strong> (<a href={SITE_URL} class="ror-link">{SITE_DOMAIN}</a>) is an independent browser-based software project — not a registered U.S. corporation with a physical office. We are committed to protecting your privacy and complying with U.S. privacy laws. This policy explains what data we collect, how we use it, and your rights.
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">
          In short: <strong class="ror-strong">We collect minimal data by design.</strong> No tracking cookies, no analytics cookies, no user accounts, and no sale or sharing of personal information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          <strong class="ror-strong">Personal information is not required.</strong> You do not need to create an account, provide a name, submit an email, or provide any personal details to use {SITE_DOMAIN}.
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">
          We store non-personal preferences — such as your Light/Dark theme selection — in your browser's <code class="ror-code">localStorage</code>. This data never leaves your device and is never transmitted to our servers.
        </p>
        <ul class="ror-ul">
          <li>Theme preference (light/dark) stored locally in your browser</li>
          <li>Standard server access logs (IP address, timestamp, URL requested, user agent, referrer, response status)</li>
          <li>Voluntarily provided information via our <a href="/contact" class="ror-link">contact form</a> (name, email, message, topic selection)</li>
          <li>No tracking, analytics, or advertising cookies used at any time</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">2. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          {SITE_DOMAIN} uses <strong class="ror-strong">no cookies</strong> for tracking, analytics, or advertising. We use <code class="ror-code">localStorage</code> for one purpose only: theme preference (light/dark mode). This setting is stored locally in your browser and is never transmitted to our servers. You can clear this data at any time by clearing site data for <code class="ror-code">{SITE_DOMAIN}</code> through your browser settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">3. No Sale or Sharing of Personal Information (California CCPA / CPRA &amp; U.S. State Privacy Rights)</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Instanten <strong class="ror-strong">does not sell or share personal information</strong> for cross-context behavioral advertising or any other commercial purpose. We comply with the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA) (Cal. Civ. Code § 1798.140) and applicable U.S. state privacy laws, including the Virginia Consumer Data Protection Act (VCDPA), Colorado Privacy Act (CPA), Connecticut Data Privacy Act (CTDPA), Texas Data Privacy and Security Act, and Oregon Consumer Privacy Act.
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Because Instanten operates as a privacy-first independent software project, we do not maintain user profiles, do not serve targeted advertisements, and do not share data with third-party analytics or advertising networks. Theme preferences remain in your browser's localStorage and are never transmitted. If you submit a contact message, the information is kept only as long as needed to respond and is never sold or shared.
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">
          If you are a California resident and wish to exercise your rights — including the right to know, correct, delete, or opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information — please submit your request through our verified <a href="/contact" class="ror-link">contact form</a> with the topic "Privacy / CCPA / DMCA inquiry." We will respond within the timelines required by applicable U.S. state law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">4. Children's Privacy (U.S. COPPA Compliance)</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Instanten complies with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA, <strong>15 U.S.C. §§ 6501–6506</strong>). The Service is not directed at children under 13 years of age, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you are a parent or guardian and believe that a child under 13 has provided personal information through our contact form, please contact us immediately through our <a href="/contact" class="ror-link">contact form</a> (select "Privacy / CCPA / DMCA inquiry") and we will delete it promptly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">5. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          We use Google Fonts for typography. You can review Google's privacy practices here: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="ror-link">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Our site links directly to official tool websites. When you visit an external tool, you leave {SITE_DOMAIN} and are subject to that site's own privacy practices. We do not control those practices and recommend reviewing their policies before using their services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">6. Data Retention</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          We retain no personal user profiles. Contact messages are kept only as long as needed to respond. Theme preferences live entirely in your browser and are deleted when you clear site data. Standard server access logs are retained only for the minimum period necessary for site security and performance monitoring.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">7. Intellectual Property &amp; DMCA Copyright Notice (17 U.S.C. § 512)</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          All original content on {SITE_DOMAIN} — including design, code, copy, guides, and original thumbnails — is owned by {SITE_NAME} or licensed under appropriate terms. Tool names, logos, descriptions, and external links belong to their respective owners.
        </p>
        <p class="ror-p">
          If you believe that content on this site infringes your copyright, please submit a DMCA copyright notice through our verified <a href="/contact" class="ror-link">contact form</a> (select "Privacy / CCPA / DMCA inquiry"). Your notice must include: (1) identification of the copyrighted work, (2) identification of the infringing material with sufficient detail, (3) your contact information, (4) a statement of good faith belief, (5) a statement of accuracy under penalty of perjury, and (6) your physical or electronic signature. We will respond promptly in accordance with 17 U.S.C. § 512.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">8. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Since we collect minimal personal data by design, there is very little to access, rectify, or delete. If you emailed us, you can request deletion of your messages by emailing <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="ror-link">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or using the contact form with the topic "Privacy / CCPA / DMCA inquiry."
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Updates will be posted on this page with a revised "Last updated" date. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ror-section">
        <h2 class="ror-h2">10. Contact</h2>
        <p class="ror-p">
          Questions about this Privacy Policy, CCPA/CPRA rights, COPPA compliance, or DMCA notices? Reach out through our verified <a href="/contact" class="ror-link">contact form</a> (topic: "Privacy / CCPA / DMCA inquiry") or email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="ror-link">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. There is no fake office address or fake U.S. phone number — only real working channels for real users.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
